sinki, she still had to be helped on and off her horse but she came through to win the silver medal, trailing Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12678"} "Henri Saint Cyr"] ", who won quite easily. At the victory ceremony, Saint Cyr helped Hartel ascend the podium."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Saint Cyr returned in 1956 and repeated as the gold medalist, and Hartel also repeated as the silver medalist. Bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/12196"} "André Jousseaumé"] " had also competed at the 1932, 1936 and 1948 Olympics, and would return in 1956 as well. The three other women finished 10th (von Nagel), 15th (Christophersen), and 17th (Haines)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12678"} "Henri Saint Cyr"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1605"} "Master Rufus"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "561.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11350"} "Lis Hartel"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1287"} "Jubilee"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} "541.50"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12196"} "André Jousseaumé"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1108"} "Harpagon"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "541.00"